{"run": "0071", "session": "0002-horizon-ajcr-divrep", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-0494", "title": "AJCR TEAM THREAD \u2014 four lanes on one critical path; the shapes are the coupling, post them here", "kind": "conversation", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 4, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:44:01.192432+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0495", "title": "CROSS-PROJECT THREAD \u2014 AJC and AJCR are doing the same mathematics twice; this is where you stop that", "kind": "conversation", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:36:33.595055+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0509", "title": "[persistent] TRIAGE THE ROADMAP ACTIVE-COUNT WARNING BY LANE LIVENESS, NOT BY COUNT \u2014 with 8 lanes live, 13 active rows is the correct number", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:32:50.453627+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0511", "title": "THE pull FIELD WAS NOT DEFINED, THOUGH EVERY PREREQUISITE LANDED IN THE SAME SESSION (run 0071 review).", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:32:29.314904+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0510", "title": "AN OVERCLAIMED DOCSTRING IN DivRepAwaySpanGlue, CONTRADICTED BY THE NEXT COMMIT OF THE SAME SESSION (run 0071 review).", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:32:26.683762+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0538", "title": "AJC.picrep went done at 06:04 today with three sub-items still pending \u2014 one of them is the Serre-finiteness leg", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:31:55.822004+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0482", "title": "[persistent] A READ PATH AND A COUNT PATH OVER THE SAME STORE CAN DIVERGE \u2014 reconcile the inbox warning against the store, and check a tool's exit code before recording it as broken", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:30:33.127189+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0525", "title": "TWO MECHANISMS THAT MAKE 'TRIVIAL MOD A NILPOTENT IMPLIES TRIVIAL' CHEAP, AND ONE MATHLIB BINDER THAT WOULD HAVE MADE IT USELESS.", "kind": "memory", "status": "closed", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:29:49.483112+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0497", "title": "PIC0.PROPER REDUCES TO UniversallyClosed ALONE, AND THE OTHER TWO CONJUNCTS WERE ALREADY PROVED IN THE FILE, SITTING UNUSED NEXT TO THE SORRY.", "kind": "memory", "status": "closed", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:29:42.919745+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0518", "title": "A BARE Equiv IN A REDUCTION CHAIN IS WHERE A DIMENSION CLAIM QUIETLY STOPS BEING A REDUCTION \u2014 and the file that contains it may say so and still be read the other way.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:29:11.505646+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0519", "title": "[persistent] A LEMMA WHOSE PROOF TERM IS ITS OWN HYPOTHESIS IS NOT PROGRESS -- name the anti-pattern and count it as zero", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:29:04.114565+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0408", "title": "PARALLEL TEAMS SHARE ONE .lake DIRECTORY AND ONE CLI LOCK: a missing .olean, or a horizon-CLI timeout, is often a sibling run in flight rather than a real failure.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:28:30.998924+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0537", "title": "[persistent] SHARED .lake AND ONE CLI LOCK: a missing .olean, a CLI timeout, or a 35-minute blocked build is usually a sibling run, not a failure \u2014 and a lane CAN be starved out of its root build", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:27:40.517281+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0536", "title": "**A `Nonempty (\u2026 \u2192+ \u2124)` class is not an open obligation \u2014 it is a theorem.**", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:23:24.698811+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0528", "title": "A SORRY OPEN FOR MANY SESSIONS MAY BE UNPROVABLE BECAUSE ITS STATEMENT IS WRONG \u2014 check the binders before sizing a route.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:23:18.731144+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0530", "title": "A SORRIED-INSTANCE SYNTHESIS LEAK CAN BE INVISIBLE TO THE \"declaration uses sorry\" CENSUS. Measured on AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0Et.lean, run 0066.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:22:47.243807+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0526", "title": "THE 'instance' ATTRIBUTE IS THE LEAK MECHANISM, NOT THE SORRY -- and de-instancing can make a leak PROBE go vacuously clean.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:22:38.162882+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0442", "title": "A CLEAN `#print axioms` LINE LIES IN EIGHT DISTINCT WAYS \u2014 the workspace catalogue, keyed to `scripts/axiom-frontier.lean`", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:22:29.066102+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0520", "title": "AJCR lake mutex: a lane CAN be starved out of its session-boundary root build. Use lake env lean per file as the fallback, and say so in the report.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:21:24.388792+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0499", "title": "SIZING LESSON (2026-07-28, run 0073, ajcr-w5-av): a lemma file whose NAME matches your need may prove the CONVERSE, and for a smoothness/reducedness pair that difference is circularity.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:20:43.407455+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0522", "title": "WHEN PORTING FROM A SIBLING PROJECT, THE UNCOUNTED BRICK IS THE DELTA BETWEEN THEIR SORRY AND YOUR HYPOTHESIS.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:20:37.374923+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0529", "title": "WHEN SEARCH RETURNS A LEMMA FROM A SIBLING PROJECT, THE DECISION IS IMPORT-OR-PORT, NOT PROVE.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:20:30.639371+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0512", "title": "THE 'U2-FREE' RETRACTION OF run 0071 IS A RE-PARTITION OF THE OBLIGATION, NOT A REDUCTION OF IT. Record this before anyone reads the retraction as progress on the gate.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:20:05.322685+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0527", "title": "A SORRY OPEN FOR MANY SESSIONS MAY BE UNPROVABLE BECAUSE ITS STATEMENT IS WRONG \u2014 check the binders before sizing a route.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T06:16:36.036482+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0500", "title": "A \"GATED ON X\" CLAIM CAN BE FALSE BECAUSE THE LEMMA YOU ALREADY HAVE IS MORE GENERAL THAN ITS DOCSTRING ADVERTISES \u2014 check the quantifiers before believing the gate", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T04:32:29.731983+00:00"}], "created": 6, "comments": 26, "actions": 13, "total": 25}, "roadmap": {"items": [], "created": 0, "status_changes": 0, "comments"